Z||000000||Indy-2M4||12-01-2001||04:36 PM||||and forgive me for any language. I was really looking forward to the get-together in Columbus, but a rash of things happened. First, we got a late start (of course mostly because of my husband, you have to understand that he is an egotistical selfish POS that doesn't care for anyone but himself and never knows how to be on time for anything). My idea to take 2 Fieros-big mistake-"liability only" on all of them and you should see the way this A**hole drives. The bastard leaves me and continues on 70 when we were supposed to get off on 270 (doesn't follow directions either). The way he was driving (MY car, this again proves he has no regard for anyone else or their property), darting in and out of cars,not using turn signals most of the time, I was having trouble keeping up with him and wasn't going to risk loosing the car to his driving not to mention scared S***less that he was going to wreck my Indy, I got lost as hell and was very late (I'm sure he was already there). By the time I got there, I was a shot basket of nerves and just about to break in tears and the F***er didn't even appologize for leaving me or didn't even bother calling me to see if I was finding my way. The SOB was probably hoping I wouldn't show so he could flirt with the Hooter's Girls (somehow, I guess I wouldn't be too surprised if he DID). I had so looked forward to this day, and then just like that, it gets shot down, thanks to a selfish F***. I'm sure he showed his good side to you all, but.....well I'll leave it at that. I hope you guys had fun. That includes you "Old Man". Just remember, it was my idea to go, and it will be the last time I EVER include you in something like this again. BTW, did YOU get lost. And my car had better be in the driveway in one piece and not a scratch on it. BTW....I will have the insurance company send me a waiver for him to sign to keep him from driving my cars. Thanks to him,my insurance is higher to carry him because of his past driving history, and the waiver is the only way the insurance company will take him off my auto policy. I am so sorry again, you guys, for any language. I tried to conceal it the best I could. <P>------------------<BR>Kathy<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_Indy_Sig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
